---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { LINKS, PERSON, RESUME_PDF_URL } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Joel Huffman, product manager in Colorado Springs, CO.">
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container about-grid">
			<div class="photo">
				<Picture
					src={headshot}
					alt="Joel Huffman, smiling, in a dark blazer and clear glasses"
					widths={[320, 480, 720]}
					sizes="(max-width: 860px) 260px, 360px"
					formats={['avif', 'webp']}
				/>
				<p class="where">📍 {PERSON.location}</p>
			</div>

			<div class="prose">
				<span class="eyebrow">About</span>
				<h1>A product manager who started on the ground floor</h1>

				<p>
					My first degree was in wind energy and turbine technology, a hands-on field about complex systems and the people
					who keep them running. Later I added a B.A.S. in IT Management and moved into software.
				</p>
				<p>
					I started at Cendyn in data quality, validating hotel property-management integration data. That work showed me
					how small data problems turn into big customer problems. I moved into business analysis and then
					product ownership, spending time at hotel front desks to watch how staff actually used our product before
					deciding what to build next.
				</p>
				<p>
					After a stint as a product analyst at American Express, I spent four years at Corporate Travel Management
					owning a global traveler-profile platform: consolidating three regional systems into one product for thousands
					of companies and millions of travelers, with the identity, permissions and compliance work that comes with
					that scale.
				</p>

				<h2>How I work</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Start with the people doing the work.</strong> The best roadmap input I’ve had came from watching someone struggle with a screen.</li>
					<li><strong>Make the business case explicit.</strong> Build vs. buy, cost of delay, savings: I write the numbers down so the decision can be challenged.</li>
					<li><strong>Ship in stages.</strong> Feature flags, beta groups and the willingness to pause something that isn’t working.</li>
					<li><strong>Use AI as a daily tool.</strong> For discovery, diagnosing issues and building working prototypes, like this site.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>What I’m looking for</h2>
				<p>{PERSON.currently} I’m especially interested in teams where platform work, data quality and good user experience have to meet.</p>

				<!-- TODO(Joel): add a short "Outside of work" paragraph: hobbies, family, what you're into in Colorado Springs. -->

				<div class="actions">
					<a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}><Icon name="mail" /> Say hello</a>
					<a class="btn btn-ghost" href={RESUME_PDF_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="download" /> Resume</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 360px 1fr;
		gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		align-items: start;
	}
	.photo {
		position: sticky;
		top: 100px;
	}
	.photo :global(img) {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: 50% 25%;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-lift);
		transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
	}
	.where {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.prose h2 {
		margin-top: 1.6em;
	}
	.actions {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.about-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.photo {
			position: static;
			width: min(260px, 70%);
			margin-inline: auto;
		}
	}
</style>
